      "text": "The Flathead Indian Reservation, set up by the 1855 Hellgate Treaty, originally covered Big Arm.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/big_arm_montana",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Big Arm has stayed rural while blending influences from the Confederated Salish and Kootenai Tribes.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/big_arm_montana",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Before 1910, the Kootenai people called the bay 'Big Arm,' and homesteaders arrived after the reservation opened.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        4
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.mtmemory.org/nodes/view/127481",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Big Arm sits on the south side of a large bay on Flathead Lake, which gave the town its name.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        8
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Big_Arm%2C_Montana",
      "category": "nature",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "text": "Flathead Lake, called Čɫq̓étkʷ by the tribes, was a sacred resource for fishing, hunting, and travel.",
